            <ArticleTitle>On the origin of the stereoselectivity in chiral amide-based ammonium ylide-mediated epoxidations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00706-016-1866-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Detailed DFT studies provide an in-depth mechanistic understanding for the use of chiral amide-based ammonium ylides in epoxidation reactions. It is shown that the used chiral auxiliary efficiently shields one face of the ylide, which thus results in an extraordinarily high stereoselectivity giving only one trans-isomer with perfect control of the absolute configuration.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="GRAPHICAL ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED"/>
            </Abstract>
